{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Performance acceptance evidence for direct close instrumentation at commit f4206fe6428d.\n\nMethod: standard-library CPU-time ABBA differential with GC disabled during measurement. The baseline and measured paths traverse the same existing close helper graph; the measured arm additionally creates the collector and exercises both outer timed phases, descendant-scope timing/counting, landing/history/diff timing/counting, verifier timing, and the existing metrics merge. Existing Git/model/I/O work is stubbed. The synthetic history contains 2,714 entries, matching this checkout's `git rev-list --count HEAD` at measurement time. Seven repeats of 1,000 loops report per-close block-average deltas; the acceptance threshold is 50 microseconds.\n\nExact command:\n\n    rtk env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -c 'exec(\"\"\"import gc\n    import statistics\n    import time\n    from types import SimpleNamespace\n    from rebar._commands import close_autoresume, close_precheck, transition_close, verify_commit\n    from rebar._engine_support import commit_impact, descendants, field_reads, resolver\n    count = 2714\n    history = \"\".join(f\"sha-{i}\\\\x1fmessage {i}\\\\x00\" for i in range(count))\n    commit_impact.subprocess.run = lambda *args, **kwargs: SimpleNamespace(returncode=0, stdout=history)\n    resolver.build_resolver_scan_index = lambda tracker: SimpleNamespace(alias_to_dirs={}, sorted_dir_names=[])\n    resolver.resolve_ticket_id = lambda value, *args, **kwargs: value\n    verify_commit.extract_ticket_refs = lambda message: []\n    descendants.list_descendants = lambda *args, **kwargs: {\"epics\": [\"epic\"], \"stories\": [\"story\"], \"tasks\": [\"task-a\", \"task-b\"], \"bugs\": [\"bug\"]}\n    field_reads.file_impact = lambda *args, **kwargs: []\n    close_precheck._union_file_impact = lambda *args, **kwargs: [\"src/example.py\"]\n    close_precheck._attached_commit_shas = lambda *args, **kwargs: []\n    close_autoresume.verify_with_auto_resume = lambda *args, **kwargs: {\"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"metrics\": {\"requests\": 1}}\n    def noop():\n        return None\n    def base():\n        noop(); noop()\n        resolved, accepted = close_precheck._resolved_completion_scope(\"ticket\", \"/tracker\")\n        close_precheck._check_work_landed(\"ticket\", resolved, accepted, \"/tracker\", \"/repo\")\n        close_autoresume.verify_with_auto_resume(\"ticket\", ref=None, repo_root=\"/repo\", cfg_root=\"/repo\")\n    def measured():\n        metrics = transition_close._new_close_metrics()\n        transition_close._timed_close_phase(metrics, \"structural_scan_ms\", noop)\n        transition_close._timed_close_phase(metrics, \"material_policy_ms\", noop)\n        resolved, accepted = close_precheck._resolved_completion_scope(\"ticket\", \"/tracker\", metrics=metrics)\n        close_precheck._check_work_landed(\"ticket\", resolved, accepted, \"/tracker\", \"/repo\", metrics=metrics)\n        close_precheck._verify_with_duration_metrics(\"ticket\", ref=None, code_root=\"/repo\", metrics=metrics)\n    for _ in range(30):\n        base(); measured()\n    loops = 1000\n    repeats = 7\n    deltas = []\n    gc.disable()\n    try:\n        for _ in range(repeats):\n            t0 = time.process_time_ns()\n            for _ in range(loops): base()\n            t1 = time.process_time_ns()\n            for _ in range(loops): measured()\n            t2 = time.process_time_ns()\n            for _ in range(loops): measured()\n            t3 = time.process_time_ns()\n            for _ in range(loops): base()\n            t4 = time.process_time_ns()\n            deltas.append(((t2-t1)+(t3-t2)-(t1-t0)-(t4-t3))/(2*loops*1000))\n    finally:\n        gc.enable()\n    ordered = sorted(deltas)\n    print(f\"complete_close_bookkeeping_cpu_abba commit_scan_count={count} repeats={repeats} loops={loops} added_us_best={min(deltas):.3f} added_us_p50={statistics.median(deltas):.3f} added_us_p90={ordered[int(0.9*(len(ordered)-1))]:.3f} added_us_worst={max(deltas):.3f} threshold_us=50\")\n    \"\"\")'\n\nExact result:\n\n    complete_close_bookkeeping_cpu_abba commit_scan_count=2714 repeats=7 loops=1000 added_us_best=20.556 added_us_p50=26.354 added_us_p90=34.404 added_us_worst=35.653 threshold_us=50\n\nResult: PASS. Every repeat's block-average delta was below 50 microseconds. No event, tracker/file read or write, Git/network/model call, tracing, worker, lock, retry, or sleep is added by the instrumented path; the benchmark replaces pre-existing expensive operations only to isolate the new bookkeeping."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787582675639473001,"uuid":"2fdffca1-58ee-48b6-bbf7-e9633ff388ae"}